      "text": "To solve the expression \\(\\sqrt[4]{2^7 \\cdot 3^3}\\), we need to simplify it step by step.\n\nFirst, we can rewrite the expression using the properties of exponents:\n\\[\n\\sqrt[4]{2^7 \\cdot 3^3} = (2^7 \\cdot 3^3)^{1/4}\n\\]\n\nNext, we apply the power of a product rule, which states that \\((xy)^n = x^n y^n\\):\n\\[\n(2^7 \\cdot 3^3)^{1/4} = 2^{7/4} \\cdot 3^{3/4}\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to express \\(2^{7/4}\\) and \\(3^{3/4}\\) in a form that can be simplified further. We can write:\n\\[\n2^{7/4} = 2^{6/4 + 1/4} = 2^{6/4} \\cdot 2^{1/4} = 2^{3/2} \\cdot 2^{1/4} = \\sqrt{2^3} \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{2} = \\sqrt{8} \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{2}\n\\]\n\\[\n3^{3/4} = 3^{2/4 + 1/4} = 3^{2/4} \\cdot 3^{1/4} = 3^{1/2} \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{3^3} = \\sqrt{3} \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{27}\n\\]\n\nCombining these, we get:\n\\[\n2^{7/4} \\cdot 3^{3/4} = \\sqrt{8} \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{2} \\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{27} = \\sqrt{8 \\cdot 3} \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{2 \\cdot 27} = \\sqrt{24} \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{54}\n\\]\n\nHowever, we need to check if we can simplify \\(\\sqrt{24}\\) and \\(\\sqrt[4]{54}\\) further. We know that:\n\\[\n24 = 4 \\cdot 6 = 2^2 \\cdot 6\n\\]\n\\[\n54 = 9 \\cdot 6 = 3^2 \\cdot 6\n\\]\n\nSo,\n\\[\n\\sqrt{24} = \\sqrt{2^2 \\cdot 6} = 2\\sqrt{6}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sqrt[4]{54} = \\sqrt[4]{3^2 \\cdot 6} = \\sqrt{3} \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{6}\n\\]\n\nBut the problem asks for the simplified form \\(a\\sqrt[4]{b}\\), and we need to ensure that the expression is in the form of a single fourth root. Let's re-evaluate the expression:\n\\[\n2^{7/4} \\cdot 3^{3/4} = 2^{3/2} \\cdot 2^{1/4} \\cdot 3^{3/4} = 2^{3/2} \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{2} \\cdot 3^{3/4}\n\\]\n\nWe need to express \\(2^{3/2}\\) as a single fourth root:\n\\[\n2^{3/2} = (2^3)^{1/2} = 8^{1/2} = \\sqrt{8} = 2\\sqrt{2}\n\\]\n\nSo, combining all parts, we get:\n\\[\n2\\sqrt{2} \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{2} \\cdot 3^{3/4} = 2\\sqrt[4]{2^3} \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{2} \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{27} = 2\\sqrt[4]{2^4 \\cdot 27} = 2\\sqrt[4]{108}\n\\]\n\nThus, the simplified form is \\(2\\sqrt[4]{108}\\), and we have \\(a = 2\\) and \\(b = 108\\). Therefore, \\(a + b = 2 + 108 = 110\\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{110}\n\\]",
